The arena allocators over every tracked model.json in the pinned producer
submodule, both normalized dialects, payload-free. Gated on ARENA_EVAL_MODELS;
run with `make arena.eval`. See bin/arena_alloc_eval.ml.

The grid is fixed here so this output is reproducible: every strategy without
search and with 10 to 800 iterations of the order search, two seeds, the
production portfolio at the same budgets, and a bounded reference minimum.

  $ ../bin/arena_alloc_eval.exe --models-dir "$ARENA_EVAL_MODELS" \
  >   --expected-models 100 --dialects native,native4d --stage normalized \
  >   --iterations 0,10,25,50,100,200,400,800 --seeds 1,2 \
  >   --reference-max-states 100000 --reference-max-depth 256 \
  >   --output eval.jsonl --models-output models.jsonl 2>/dev/null

Coverage, and why each dialect that was not evaluated was refused.

  $ grep '"type":"coverage"' eval.jsonl
  {"type":"coverage","dialect":"native","expected":100,"attempted":100,"evaluated":100,"refused":0,"prerequisite":0,"failed":0}
  {"type":"coverage","dialect":"native4d","expected":100,"attempted":100,"evaluated":97,"refused":3,"prerequisite":0,"failed":0}
  $ grep -o '"model":"[^"]*","dialect":"[^"]*","type":"dialect","status":"refused","stage":"[^"]*","reason":"[^"]*"' eval.jsonl
  "model":"bat_resnext26ts","dialect":"native4d","type":"dialect","status":"refused","stage":"native4d_convert","reason":"outside_dialect_domain"
  "model":"eca_halonext26ts","dialect":"native4d","type":"dialect","status":"refused","stage":"native4d_convert","reason":"outside_dialect_domain"
  "model":"lambda_resnet26t","dialect":"native4d","type":"dialect","status":"refused","stage":"native4d_convert","reason":"outside_dialect_domain"

Per model and dialect, summed over element kinds, in bytes: the proven lower
bound and the best upper bound (equal when the minimum is proven), then each
column's arena in the order the first row names. A column is
`<strategy>` (one placement pass), `<strategy>+improve@<iterations>/<seed>`
(that pass, then the order search) or `portfolio@<iterations>/<seed>` (the
production planner).

